Subject: Temporarily define the retail initial rendered-impostor count
Upstream-base: 11c0bc65ad2ec21431c5d74f1ac4cbc1e3e2e2c3
Classification: TEMPORARY unfinished-source data definition (native only); remove when upstream defines it.

NonMatching Game/Render/ImpostorManager.cpp declares sInitialRenderedImpostorCount
extern and reads it while starting each impostor render pass, but no source
unit defines it. The FE model owners (0552) make that pass reachable through
FEModelManager::Render, so the module fails to load on the unresolved object.

Retail evidence: config/R4QE01/symbols.txt lists
sInitialRenderedImpostorCount = .sdata:0x806DF434 (global object, size 4),
directly after this unit's sDefaultImpostorSizeScale (0x806DF430, 1.0f). The
owner's retail main.dol (SHA-1 e96d2298067b70652752145b4e63644e6e1b1560, DOL
section 13 file offset 0x568534) holds BE 00000000 there. Define it in native
builds with exactly that value; the console declaration is unchanged.
Removal condition: an upstream ImpostorManager.cpp (or other unit) defines the
object; then drop this patch and confirm the native link takes the source one.

--- a/src/Game/Render/ImpostorManager.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Render/ImpostorManager.cpp
@@ -19,7 +19,15 @@
 static int sImpostorAlphaTestReference = 0x80;
 static int sImpostorUpdatePeriod = 1;
 static float sDefaultImpostorSizeScale = 1.0f;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// Temporary unfinished-source definition: retail main.dol (SHA-1
+// e96d2298067b70652752145b4e63644e6e1b1560) holds this global object at
+// .sdata 0x806DF434 = BE 00000000, after sDefaultImpostorSizeScale. Remove
+// when the reconstructed unit defines it.
+int sInitialRenderedImpostorCount = 0;
+#else
 extern int sInitialRenderedImpostorCount;
+#endif
 
